    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "These relations form the N = 2 SUSY algebra. It describes SUSY quantum mechanics [38,6]. We can also view it as generators of a Z2-grading of a Hilbert space."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 2,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 117.629, 684.263, 325.934, 695.172 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Using these generators it is easy to see that"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 3,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 275.189, 652.023, 350.202, 665.843 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "S = q or S = q†"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 4,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 101.265, 620.542, 326.347, 631.451 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "realizes nilpotent S’s. On the other hand when"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 5,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 275.771, 588.681, 350.119, 599.59 ],
    "font" : "CMMI10",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "S = b or S = f,"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 6,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 101.265, 521.593, 524.626, 567.73 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "we obtain projector S’s. These operators help construct the constant Yij operator SiSj. They can satisfy either of the three conditions set in (3.9). The corresponding Hamiltonians are either given by (3.4) or (3.8)."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 7,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 101.265, 486.365, 524.625, 514.888 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "The operator Yij = SiTj is Baxterized when either one of ST = 0 or TS = 0 is satisfied. This is easily realized using the SUSY generators4 as"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 9,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 282.161, 438.959, 291.858, 479.672 ],
    "font" : "CMEX10",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : ""
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 12,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 291.858, 369.658, 359.506, 465.114 ],
    "font" : "CMMI10",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "S = q, T = b S = q†, T = f S = b, T = q† S = f, T = q. S = b, T = f,"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
